        "original_id": "359e5cc1-76d5-5b79-ba38-5d26792dccdd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: George Frideric Handel\n- Products: Keyboard glockenspiel, Keyboard suite in D minor (HWV 437)\n- Works: Saul\n- Topics: Musical influences, Baroque music\n\nFacts:\n- George Frideric Handel composed the Keyboard suite in D minor (HWV 437) for solo keyboard, specifically harpsichord, between 1703 and 1706.\n- George Frideric Handel was strongly influenced by the great composers of the Italian Baroque and by the middle-German polyphonic choral tradition.\n- George Frideric Handel first used the keyboard glockenspiel in the oratorio Saul in 1739.",
